## Interface: 16001
## Title: Efficient Quests
## Notes: A step-by-step leveling guide for the Forever client.
## Version: 0.3.0
## OptionalDeps: FlareUI, TomTom, QuestieDB
## SavedVariables: EfficientQuestsDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: EfficientQuestsCharacter

# The embedded libraries load first, in dependency order: HereBeDragons
# needs LibStub and CallbackHandler. The pins part of HereBeDragons is
# not embedded, because pins draw on maps.
Libs/LibStub/LibStub.lua
Libs/CallbackHandler-1.0/CallbackHandler-1.0.lua
Libs/HereBeDragons/HereBeDragons-2.0.lua
Core.lua
CharacterStore.lua

# The generated data tables copied verbatim from Trailwright (see
# THIRD_PARTY.md): the quest data, the Path, and the dungeon guide stops.
# They are plain data, so they load before any code that reads them.
QuestData.lua
PathData.lua
DungeonGuides.lua

# The data store checks the shape of the tables above at load time and
# exposes the data snapshot identity for the status command.
DataStore.lua

# The options panel is a window of our own; it opens from the step window
# and from the /eq command, so it builds itself only on first open.
Options.lua

# The menu opens beside the step window, which hands itself over as the
# anchor of Menu.Open. Without an anchor it sits at a fixed screen spot.
Menu.lua

# Interface.lua is the old window module. It stays in this folder as a
# frozen reference for the new step window and is never loaded.
